AB  - Accurate defect detection in automotive battery sealing nails is vital for safety and reliability. Traditional methods combine two-dimensional (2D) vision for localization with three-dimensional (3D) vision for measurement, resulting in complex workflows and reduced efficiency. We propose Local Graph Attention for Semantic Segmentation (LGASS), an end-to-end 3D point cloud segmentation model. LGASS processes raw point cloud data from structured-light systems, performing simultaneous defect localization and geometric quantification in a single stage. By leveraging a graph attention mechanism in an encoder–decoder architecture, LGASS captures local geometric features and long-range dependencies, excelling on industrial metallic surfaces. Experiments show LGASS achieves 99.47% Overall Accuracy (OA), 92.37% mean Accuracy (mAcc), and 79.23% mean Intersection over Union (mIoU), offering a robust solution for automated sealing nail inspection.
